WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.800
- So let's talk about
something serious though,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.633
this is amazing.

00:00:02.633 --> 00:00:04.792
So Six Degrees, your organization-

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:05.625
- Yep.

00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:06.690
- We did something earlier today,

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.760
but talk about, what's the purpose?

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.593
Why did you wanna do this?

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:13.140
- Well Sixdegrees.org is
a charitable organization

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.065
we started in 2017.

00:00:15.065 --> 00:00:20.065
And this 2024 is the 40th anniversary

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.340
of a certain movie that I did-

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.300
- Where there might
have been some dancing.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.222
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:29.634
- There might have been
barn dancing going on.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:30.467
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:35.090
- And so we launched this
initiative to build 40,000 kits,

00:00:36.929 --> 00:00:40.395
and these are kits that are in bags

00:00:40.395 --> 00:00:43.530
or backpacks that get
distributed to people

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.540
that need essential items.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.636
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:48.870
- Whether they be not doing well,

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.320
struggling, unhoused,
whatever it happens to be.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.110
Children sometimes who can't afford them

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.898
or going off to school.

00:00:56.898 --> 00:01:01.350
So today, with your beautiful crowd,

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.840
we actually built 200 bags.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.190
- Super cool man.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.785
Yeah, and let's talk about your podcast.

00:01:06.785 --> 00:01:09.391
So this is Six Degrees
with Kevin Bacon, right?

00:01:09.391 --> 00:01:10.224
- [Kevin] Yeah.

00:01:10.224 --> 00:01:11.496
- [Kelly] What do y'all talk about?

00:01:11.496 --> 00:01:16.033
- It's a podcast where
in the first half of it

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:19.514
I discuss with celebrities,

00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:23.850
whether they are actors or musicians,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.250
dancers, people from sports,

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.201
reality television, comedians.

00:01:28.201 --> 00:01:30.120
We just kind of shoot the breeze,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.374
we talk about whatever
connections we might have,

00:01:32.374 --> 00:01:36.450
either in terms of having
worked together or whatever.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.760
And the second half of it is

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.200
we talk about the organizations

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.250
that they are connected to.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.330
Either they're on the board

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:44.430
or it's a foundation that
they've actually started.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.862
And we bring the person on to the podcast

00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:50.280
who runs their foundation so
that they get a microphone

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.538
in front of them, someone that doesn't-

00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:52.371
- [Kelly] Get the spotlight.

00:01:52.371 --> 00:01:53.241
- Get the spotlight, yeah.

00:01:53.241 --> 00:01:55.900
And so it's a lot about

00:01:56.838 --> 00:01:59.040
bringing some attention to things

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.540
that celebrities care about

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.010
other than the clothes that they wear

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.150
or the restaurants that they go to.

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:03.983
- Yeah.

00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:04.816
Speaking of good causes,

00:02:04.816 --> 00:02:06.720
tomorrow is Giving Tuesday, everybody.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.220
A movement that encourages people

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.530
and organizations to positively transform

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.820
communities around the world.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.110
We can do it.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.200
So Building Kits by Kevin Bacon campaign.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.760
So how can people get involved

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.593
other than showing up

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:19.470
to be an audience member at my show?

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.385
- Well that's a great start.

00:02:22.385 --> 00:02:24.699
There's a few different ways.

00:02:24.699 --> 00:02:27.720
One is that if you have an organization,

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.134
wherever it is in the country,

00:02:30.134 --> 00:02:35.134
that has a need, even
during this bag building

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.730
someone reached out to
our Six Degrees person,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.777
and said "I got an organization in Seattle

00:02:40.777 --> 00:02:42.840
"that could really use
something like this going on."

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:43.673
- Yeah.

00:02:43.673 --> 00:02:45.515
- So that's one way you
can go to SixDegrees.org,

00:02:45.515 --> 00:02:48.240
and connect with us that way.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.730
You can also donate for sure.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.290
We need to raise money-

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.180
- [Kelly] To buy the essentials.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:54.858
- To buy the essentials, to buy the bags.

00:02:54.858 --> 00:02:57.720
We do have as many corporate sponsorships

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.603
and partnerships as we possibly can.

00:02:59.603 --> 00:03:02.310
You know, the Bomba socks
today came from Bomba.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.330
- I love Bomba.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.400
- For instance.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.549
And the third way is in your communities

00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:10.100
if you hear about this going on

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.970
to just volunteer.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.803
And it doesn't cost you anything,

00:03:13.803 --> 00:03:16.140
you show up, you take the things,

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:16.980
you put 'em in the bag,

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.750
and it's a great sense of satisfaction

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.529
that you feel when you...

00:03:20.529 --> 00:03:23.010
My brother and I were down in D.C.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.510
playing a Bacon Brothers Show,

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.238
and we showed up, it took us
whatever, an hour of our day

00:03:28.238 --> 00:03:30.276
where we're sitting around
waiting for sound check

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:33.480
to just go and hang out with some people,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.950
and put some stuff in some bags,

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.230
and then the satisfaction
of turning around,

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.165
and seeing 300 bags that
are gonna go to kids

00:03:39.165 --> 00:03:41.855
that are struggling in the D.C. area.

00:03:41.855 --> 00:03:43.041
It's a great feeling.

00:03:43.041 --> 00:03:44.310
- Absolutely.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.560
Well, as we mentioned
earlier before the show

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.990
our audience, Kevin and I all got together

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.000
to help out with his
Building Kits Campaign,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.331
so here's how that went.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.579
(gentle music)

00:03:54.579 --> 00:03:55.470
(crowd cheers)

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.303
I'm excited.

00:03:56.303 --> 00:03:57.492
- Thank you so much for doing this, Kelly.

00:03:57.492 --> 00:03:58.980
- [Kelly] I think this is
the coolest thing ever.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.042
We're building things, right?

00:04:00.042 --> 00:04:01.625
- [Kevin] Yeah, we're building bags.

00:04:01.625 --> 00:04:02.981
- [Producer] So they
don't know you're coming.

00:04:02.981 --> 00:04:05.382
- Well they do now.

00:04:05.382 --> 00:04:06.447
Woo.

00:04:06.447 --> 00:04:09.387
(crowd cheering)

00:04:09.387 --> 00:04:10.220
We're so stoked you're here.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.120
We're excited for the show obviously too,

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.892
but I'm super excited, I
never got to do anything

00:04:13.892 --> 00:04:15.390
like this yet, so I'm excited.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.850
This was all Kevin's idea, by the way.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.230
It's amazing 'cause he had this idea

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.150
for us to pack bags,
like all the essentials,

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.260
like toothpaste, deodorant,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.130
and we had the audience,

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.330
we already have all these people here.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.163
What's up everybody?

00:04:25.163 --> 00:04:27.386
- [Kevin] Something like
this Is very, very simple,

00:04:27.386 --> 00:04:28.219
and it is-
- But effective.

00:04:28.219 --> 00:04:29.052
- Effective, yeah.

00:04:29.052 --> 00:04:30.728
And it brings people together.

00:04:30.728 --> 00:04:32.580
- Everybody, you just put one thing

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.810
from each basket, right?

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.643
- Yep.

00:04:34.643 --> 00:04:35.514
One thing from each basket.

00:04:35.514 --> 00:04:36.390
- Look at you right now.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.078
- They're all essential
things that people need.

00:04:38.078 --> 00:04:40.320
- I was one that needed
help when I was younger.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.153
- Oh.

00:04:41.153 --> 00:04:41.986
- So we needed the help,

00:04:41.986 --> 00:04:42.819
we needed the essentials,

00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:43.652
we needed all that stuff.

00:04:43.652 --> 00:04:44.790
- This is awesome.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.020
- Why don't you guys come down this side,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:46.992
and then we can just
make an assembly line,

00:04:46.992 --> 00:04:48.408
and just pass them down.

00:04:48.408 --> 00:04:49.440
- Oh yeah.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.490
Y'all come down this way.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.445
Here, I'll go down here.

00:04:51.445 --> 00:04:52.403
- Thank you.

00:04:52.403 --> 00:04:53.289
Thank you.

00:04:53.289 --> 00:04:54.122
Thank you.

00:04:54.122 --> 00:04:56.670
We've also put in a handwritten note

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.655
of any kind of inspiration that-

00:04:58.655 --> 00:04:59.488
- Okay.

00:04:59.488 --> 00:05:01.196
- You can find.

00:05:01.196 --> 00:05:02.039
- I love this.

00:05:02.039 --> 00:05:03.385
I do this for the guests.

00:05:03.385 --> 00:05:04.290
- Just hang in there.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.150
- When our recipients receive these gifts

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.790
with a handwritten note from
the person that packed them

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.225
that shows them that somebody
really cares, it's powerful.

00:05:12.225 --> 00:05:15.042
It reminds the recipient
that there's a real person

00:05:15.042 --> 00:05:16.980
on the other side of those kits.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.870
- It's just another detail for people

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.550
who are maybe just having a rough day

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:21.930
or rough time in their life.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.640
- Hey guys, thank you so much.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.510
This was all Kevin,

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.886
he was the one who came up with this.

00:05:25.886 --> 00:05:27.495
(crowd cheers)

00:05:27.495 --> 00:05:30.340
Thank you for being a
part of it this morning.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:31.920
- Thank you all so much.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:32.753
Appreciate it.

00:05:32.753 --> 00:05:33.586
Thank you.

00:05:33.586 --> 00:05:34.419
Thank you for your work.

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:35.600
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.721
- All right, so let's
talk to some of the people

00:05:37.721 --> 00:05:39.387
who helped do the bags this morning.

00:05:39.387 --> 00:05:40.680
I'm gonna start with Britney.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.225
So, Britney, what was the
experience like for you?

00:05:43.225 --> 00:05:44.932
- Well, Kelly, I really enjoyed

00:05:44.932 --> 00:05:47.310
working with you and Kevin this morning

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:48.600
building the bags.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.210
As a military spouse we
just love coming together

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.406
for one mission for Giving Tuesday,

00:05:52.406 --> 00:05:54.150
to intentionally give back

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:55.471
and connect our communities.

00:05:55.471 --> 00:05:57.780
My favorite part of this morning

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.550
was adding the person note in there

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.586
to really make it add that personal touch.

00:06:01.586 --> 00:06:03.900
Mine said "You matter" on it,

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.160
and I feel like something simple

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:05.993
is good.

00:06:05.993 --> 00:06:06.826
- Absolutely.

00:06:06.826 --> 00:06:08.280
Thank you for your family's
service, that's amazing,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.310
thank you.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:10.143
(audience applauding)

00:06:10.143 --> 00:06:10.976
Thank you, Britney.

00:06:10.976 --> 00:06:12.660
Theresa also wanted to
share her experience,

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.496
so, Theresa, why don't you
tell us what it was like.

00:06:14.496 --> 00:06:18.750
- So the experience by far was
very welcoming and warming.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.902
This really resonated with me.

00:06:20.902 --> 00:06:23.551
Growing up I was in a
single parent household,

00:06:23.551 --> 00:06:26.400
and we also depended on charity

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.140
and donations and (indistinct)

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:28.973
and all that.

00:06:28.973 --> 00:06:30.180
And one of the things

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.023
that I really liked was the comment card

00:06:32.023 --> 00:06:34.602
because we can give and we can receive,

00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:36.696
but words of wisdom,

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.520
just writing something

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.595
and saying "Keep the faith,

00:06:39.595 --> 00:06:41.287
"everything's gonna be okay,

00:06:41.287 --> 00:06:42.120
"God's with you."

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:42.953
- Encouragement, yeah.

00:06:42.953 --> 00:06:45.058
- And the encouragement
goes further sometimes

00:06:45.058 --> 00:06:47.280
than just actually
receiving a pair of socks.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.317
- Yeah, somebody took
the time to write it.

00:06:48.317 --> 00:06:49.350
- [Theresa] Exactly.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.910
- It's not an email or anything
like that, it's personal.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.080
- Exactly.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.807
Coming here was just amazing.

00:06:53.807 --> 00:06:55.230
- That's so funny you pointed it out,

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.610
but I feel like it is a lot of people,

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.538
when you grow up without

00:06:57.538 --> 00:06:59.340
then you know what that's like.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:00.173
- [Theresa] Exactly.

00:07:00.173 --> 00:07:01.680
- So when you're blessed then you know

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.720
that you need to give
because you were that person

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:04.553
on the other side.

00:07:04.553 --> 00:07:05.386
- Exactly.

00:07:05.386 --> 00:07:06.260
- I mean it's kind of odd,

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.813
but I'm almost really thankful for it

00:07:07.813 --> 00:07:09.960
because I understand the need.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.910
So it's really important thing

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.235
that not everybody gets,

00:07:13.235 --> 00:07:15.600
which you're kind of happy about,

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.680
but then you're also like

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.033
hey, think outside yourself.

00:07:18.033 --> 00:07:19.198
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:19.198 --> 00:07:20.820
Before we get to break,

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:23.441
can you tell me what was
going on in that podcast clip?

00:07:23.441 --> 00:07:24.439
You wife was in it.

00:07:24.439 --> 00:07:27.660
- Yeah, that was kind of a special episode

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.460
where she was the guest,

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.400
and we highlighted
actually our foundation,

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.536
Sixdegrees.org-

00:07:33.536 --> 00:07:34.369
- [Kelly] Together.

00:07:34.369 --> 00:07:37.252
- And Stacy Houston who runs
the foundation was there.

00:07:37.252 --> 00:07:41.100
And it was fun to...

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.050
It was unusual to-

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.770
- Have you ever interviewed her?

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.540
- No, no, I have not.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.373
- Yeah.

00:07:46.373 --> 00:07:48.810
- No, I mean unless we're
talking about breakfast.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.000
- But I didn't know if a magazine ever...

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.920
You know how sometimes they have stars

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:52.860
interview stars?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.693
I didn't know if they'd ever done that.

00:07:53.693 --> 00:07:54.526
- I don't think so.

00:07:54.526 --> 00:07:55.733
No, I don't think they've
ever asked us to do that.

00:07:55.733 --> 00:07:58.413
And we don't do that
much together, frankly.

00:07:58.413 --> 00:08:00.210
I mean we do everything together,

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.043
but we don't-

00:08:01.043 --> 00:08:01.876
- I appreciate that though.

00:08:01.876 --> 00:08:02.709
You have your separate lives, that's cool.

00:08:02.709 --> 00:08:04.410
That's important.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.640
That's why you're still married.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:06.473
- Maybe, yeah.

00:08:06.473 --> 00:08:07.306
(audience laughing)

00:08:07.306 --> 00:08:08.160
Maybe, yeah.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:08.993
- Independence.

00:08:08.993 --> 00:08:10.366
(audience applauding)

00:08:10.366 --> 00:08:12.630
Well, let's take a short break everybody.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.250
Let's check out Kevin's podcast,

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:15.372
Six Degrees with Kevin Bacon

00:08:15.372 --> 00:08:16.717
wherever you get your podcasts,

00:08:16.717 --> 00:08:18.076
and go online to find out how

00:08:18.076 --> 00:08:20.760
you can join Kevin and Six
Degrees in their campaign

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.403
to provide 40,000 essential care kits.

